## 🔵 Priority 6: CAC & Payback Period (HIGH EFFORT, STRATEGIC)

### Why This Matters

User growth is slowing. Why?

Hypothesis: Customer Acquisition Cost (CAC) is rising, making it harder to acquire users profitably.

### What You'd Need

- Marketing spend data (by channel, by month)
- Attribution model (which marketing created which users?)
- Not available in current dataset

### What You'd Build

```sql
SELECT month,
       marketing_spend,
       new_users_acquired,
       (marketing_spend / new_users_acquired) as cac,
       (user_lifetime_value / cac) as payback_months
FROM marketing_metrics
ORDER BY month
```

### Output: CAC Trend

```
Month    | Spend | New Users | CAC   | Payback (months)
---------|-------|-----------|-------|----------
2025-06  | 500M  | 100K      | 5K   | 4
2025-07  | 550M  | 90K       | 6.1K | 5
...
2026-06  | 800M  | 60K       | 13.3K| 8
2026-07  | 850M  | 50K       | 17K  | 10+
```

### What It Tells You

- CAC rising + New users falling = Acquisition is becoming less efficient
- Long payback period = Can't afford to keep acquiring

### Effort: 3-4 hours (need to build attribution model)

### Expected Impact: HIGH (but requires external data)

This explains **why** user growth is slowing. Without it, you're guessing.

